            "description": "Watch Charleston Battery vs Sacramento Republic highlights and goals from USL Championship on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on July 18, 2026. The USL Championship showdown between Charleston Battery and Sacramento Republic on July 18, 2026 , proved to be a high-stakes battle of endurance and discipline. Fans at the stadium witnessed a game where the momentum swung violently in the second half, leaving both sides breathless as the tactical battle unfolded. Breakthrough in the Second Half After a tightly contested opening period that saw both defenses holding firm, the deadlock was finally broken shortly after the restart. In the 49th minute, Sacramento Republic forward F. W. Ajago clinical finish put the visitors ahead, capitalize on a well-timed assist from J. Timmer . The goal forced Charleston Battery to increase their attacking intensity, leading to a series of physical encounters across the pitch. As the match entered its final quarter, the referee began to play a more prominent role. A. Essel of Sacramento picked up a yellow card in the 70th minute as the visitors tried to protect their slim lead. However, the pressure from the home side eventually told when they were awarded a penalty just minutes later, shifting the energy of the entire stadium. Drama and Red Cards In the 73rd minute, E. Ycaza stepped up to the spot and calmly converted the penalty to level the score at 1-1. The goal sparked immediate chaos; Ycaza himself was cautioned with a yellow card in the 75th minute, but the biggest turning point followed seconds later. F. W. Ajago , who had earlier been the hero for Sacramento, was shown a straight red card, leaving his team to navigate the closing stages with only ten men. Despite the numerical advantage, Charleston Battery struggled to find a late winner against a resilient Sacramento backline. The match concluded with another caution, this time for M. Berry in the 93rd minute, bringing an end to a fiery contest defined by its emotional swings and late-game disciplinary drama."
